export function edaView(e,current,esc){
 const n=x=>Number(x).toLocaleString('en-US'),p=(a,b)=>(100*a/b).toFixed(1)+'%',f=x=>x===null?'Unknown':Number(x).toFixed(2);
 const bars=(values,max)=>values.map(([label,value])=>`<div class="eda-bar"><span>${esc(label)}</span><div><i style="width:${100*value/(max||Math.max(...values.map(x=>x[1]))||1)}%"></i></div><b>${n(value)}</b></div>`).join('');
 return `<div class="page-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">EXPLORATORY DATA ANALYSIS</div><h1>What the actual records show.</h1><p>Recomputed from the same refreshed match data used in the explorer. Descriptive associations, not causal fatigue effects.</p></div><button class="button secondary" id="export-eda">Export EDA JSON</button></div>
 <div class="stats-grid"><div class="stat"><div class="stat-top">Unique records</div><div class="stat-value">${n(e.total)}</div><div class="stat-bottom">${n(current.audit.duplicates)} duplicate rows removed</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="stat-top">Standard completed</div><div class="stat-value">${n(e.completed)}</div><div class="stat-bottom">${n(e.nonstandard)} non-standard / unplayed records</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="stat-top">Players</div><div class="stat-value">${n(e.players.length)}</div><div class="stat-bottom">Completed singles only</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="stat-top">Source date range</div><div style="font-size:19px;margin:20px 0">${e.source_date_range.join(' → ')}</div><div class="stat-bottom">Mixed date semantics; not exact match times</div></div></div>
 <div class="research-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Missingness: all ${n(e.total)} records</h2><p class="subtext">Duration outside 20–600 minutes is treated as missing. No zero imputation.</p>${bars(Object.entries(e.missing).map(([k,v])=>[k+' · '+p(v.missing,v.total),v.missing]),e.total)}<p class="footnote">Missingness can depend on tournament and tour; complete-case duration estimates may be biased. Missing duration is not zero workload.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Duration distribution</h2><p class="subtext">Standard completed matches with recorded minutes; bins share the same scale.</p>${['ATP','WTA'].map(t=>`<h3>${t} · n = ${n(e.tours[t].duration.n)}</h3>${bars(e.tours[t].duration_bins.map(x=>[x.label+' min',x.n]),Math.max(...Object.values(e.tours).flatMap(x=>x.duration_bins.map(b=>b.n))))}`).join('')}</section></div>
 <section class="panel" style="margin-bottom:24px"><h2>Tour comparison and outcomes</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Tour</th><th>Completed</th><th>Minutes: Q1 / median / Q3</th><th>95th percentile</th><th>Missing duration</th><th>Lower-ranked winner</th><th>Full-length match</th></tr></thead><tbody>${Object.entries(e.tours).map(([t,x])=>`<tr><td>${t}</td><td>${n(x.completed)}</td><td>${x.duration.q1} / ${x.duration.median} / ${x.duration.q3}</td><td>${f(x.duration.p95)}</td><td>${n(x.missing_duration)} (${p(x.missing_duration,x.completed)})</td><td>${n(x.upsets)} / ${n(x.ranked_n)} (${p(x.upsets,x.ranked_n)})</td><td>${p(x.long_matches,x.completed)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="footnote">Upsets require two known, unequal positive rankings. Full-length means 3 sets in best-of-3 or 5 in best-of-5. ATP contains different match formats, so raw tour duration comparisons are confounded by format. Winner-oriented rows cannot define a useful 100% winner-rate model.</p></section>
 <div class="research-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>Surface composition</h2>${Object.entries(e.tours).map(([t,x])=>`<h3>${t}</h3>${bars(Object.entries(x.surfaces))}`).join('')}<p class="footnote">Counts refer to standard completed matches. These distributions reflect source coverage and scheduling, not randomly sampled conditions.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Recorded season workload</h2><p>Player match counts: median <b>${e.workload.median}</b>, IQR <b>${e.workload.q1}–${e.workload.q3}</b>, maximum <b>${e.workload.max}</b>. Many players have only a small number of observed matches.</p>${bars([...e.players].sort((a,b)=>b.recorded_minutes-a.recorded_minutes).slice(0,8).map(x=>[x.player+' · '+x.duration_available+'/'+x.matches+' timed',x.recorded_minutes]))}<p class="footnote">Bars show recorded minutes, not true total effort. Each match contributes to both participants. Doubles, qualifying, practice, travel, injury and recovery are not measured. More wins mechanically create more opportunities to accumulate workload.</p></section></div>
 <section class="panel" style="margin-bottom:24px"><h2>Correlations and fatigue proxies</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Tour</th><th>Duration vs games · Pearson r (n)</th><th>Duration vs sets · Pearson r (n)</th></tr></thead><tbody>${Object.entries(e.tours).map(([t,x])=>`<tr><td>${t}</td><td>${f(x.duration_games.r)} (${n(x.duration_games.n)})</td><td>${f(x.duration_sets.r)} (${n(x.duration_sets.n)})</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p>Player season matches vs observed win rate: r = <b>${f(e.player_workload_win.r)}</b>, n = ${e.player_workload_win.n} players. This is strongly affected by strength, selection and advancement; it does not show that playing more causes winning.</p><p>Duration, sets and games are overlapping exposure proxies. Their strong correlations do not establish physiological fatigue. Current-match minutes, games and sets are observed after play and must never predict that same match.</p></section>
 <section class="panel"><h2>Leakage and interpretation checklist</h2><p>For predictive work, orient players independently of the winner, compute workload strictly from earlier rounds, split by time and event, fit preprocessing only on training data, and keep mirrored rows in the same split. Do not use final-season totals or future rounds as pre-match features.</p><p>The source date mixes match day and event start. Exact rest hours and 7/14-day workload cannot be reliably inferred, so this analysis does not report them. Same-event prior minutes are a proxy with incomplete qualifying history. Repeated players and tournaments require clustered uncertainty; the correlations above have no causal confidence intervals.</p><p>The research model remains frozen at 22 October 2026. Its held-out test had 174 matches; adding workload did not improve log loss (0.6512 → 0.6572). That historical evaluation is not a test on this refreshed dataset.</p><p><a href="https://stats.tennismylife.org/tennis-match-database" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source documentation ↗</a> · Provider-supplied records, not independently verified against every official match. No claim of full tour or full-season completeness.</p></section>`;
}
